  "title": "Reading — Words, Lines, and a First Passage",
  "drivablePrefix": 3,
  "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:b9a4d25e28f8090a",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "LA-C58-labels",
      "sequence": 1630,
      "title": "(reading) — six words, each one already a claim",
      "headword": "(reading)",
      "romanization": "(reading)",
      "gloss": "six words read cold — and the one thing a Latin word tells you before you know the sentence",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:b5dcd2bff51e1914",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Every word below you have met. Not one is new."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is new is that nothing surrounds them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "comprehension",
          "title": "Reading",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "aqua liber schola magister discipulus oculus."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Read down the list once, without stopping."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Again, and notice that five of the six end in -us, -a or -er, and that you know what that ending means."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "An English word standing alone tells you almost nothing about its job. Book could be the thing doing or the thing done to."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Liber cannot. That ending says it is the one doing, before any sentence has been built around it. A Latin noun carries its job with it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That is what makes Latin readable in a way its word order is not. The endings do the work English does with position, and they do it one word at a time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "the six words down the list, once, without stopping",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the six words down the list, once, without stopping]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "repeat",
              "times": 2,
              "source": "[REPEAT x2]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "LA-C58-labels-teacher",
              "prompt": "Which word is the teacher?",
              "assesses": [
                "LA-SKILL-READ-LABELS"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 12,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "magister",
                "the teacher"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "magister.",
                "incorrect": "magister -- the teacher."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "How many of the six were new? (None.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does a Latin ending tell you that an English word cannot? (Its job — before the sentence exists.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "LA-C58-phrases",
      "sequence": 1640,
      "title": "(reading) — six lines, two of them one word",
      "headword": "(reading)",
      "romanization": "(reading)",
      "gloss": "six lines you would say at a door — and the two that are one word each",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:5dfe829f195afdd5",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The last lesson gave you words alone. These are whole lines."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You have said every one of them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "comprehension",
          "title": "Reading",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Salvē! Valē! Nōmen meum est Marcus. Ego sum discipulus. Iterum! Bonus est."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Read down once, without stopping."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Again — and notice that two of the six are a single word, and that both of them are things you say to somebody."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Salvē and Valē are commands. Be well. Be strong. A Roman greeting and a Roman farewell are both orders, which is why neither needs anything around it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Bonus est has no subject on the page at all. Latin puts the person in the verb, so est is already he is or it is, and the sentence is complete with two words."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That is the second thing reading Latin asks of you: expect the subject to be missing, and expect the verb to have it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "the six lines, once, in order, without stopping",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the six lines, once, in order, without stopping]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "repeat",
              "times": 2,
              "source": "[REPEAT x2]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "LA-C58-phrases-farewell",
              "prompt": "Which line would you read as you leave?",
              "assesses": [
                "LA-SKILL-READ-PHRASES"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 12,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "vale",
                "valē",
                "valē!",
                "farewell"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Valē!",
                "incorrect": "Valē! -- be strong, and so, farewell."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "How many of the six were new? (None.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Where is the subject of Bonus est? (Inside the verb.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "LA-C58-prima-lectio",
      "sequence": 1650,
      "title": "(reading) — the first passage",
      "headword": "(reading)",
      "romanization": "(reading)",
      "gloss": "the first passage — forty-two words of Latin in a row, and not one of them new",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:b1e6371e84df1fe7",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Six words, then six lines. Now twelve of them together."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Forty-two words, and not one of them is new."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "comprehension",
          "title": "Reading",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Salvē! Nōmen meum est Marcus. Ego sum discipulus. Magister meus bonus est. Liber meus bonus est. Ego legō et bibō. Amīcus meus est discipulus. Schola bona est. Prīmus liber bonus est. Sextus liber bonus est. Iterum legō, quia liber bonus est. Valē!"
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Read it once without stopping. Do not translate as you go — let the sentences arrive."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Now read it again, and look at where est falls."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Nearly every line ends in est. That is not a habit of this passage; it is how Latin was written. The verb goes last, and the reader holds everything before it open until it arrives."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two lines break the pattern on purpose. Nōmen meum est Marcus puts est in the middle, because the name is the point and Latin moves what matters. And the last full line is the longest, because quia hangs a whole reason off a sentence that was already complete."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Notice also bonus, bona, bonus — the same word three times, changing to match what it describes. You are reading agreement, not being told about it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This is the first whole passage the book has asked you to hold at once, and it works because everything in it was paid for."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "the passage aloud, once, without stopping",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the passage aloud, once, without stopping]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "repeat",
              "times": 2,
              "source": "[REPEAT x2]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "LA-C58-prima-lectio-why",
              "prompt": "Why does he read again?",
              "assesses": [
                "LA-SKILL-CONNECTED-READING"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 15,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "because the book is good",
                "quia liber bonus est",
                "the book is good"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Quia liber bonus est.",
                "incorrect": "Quia liber bonus est -- because the book is good."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Where does a Latin sentence usually keep its verb? (Last.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Why is it schola bona and not schola bonus? (The adjective agrees — and you read it before anyone explained it.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "findings": []
}
